.TH OPENNOVELLA 1 "" "OpenNovella @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opennovella \- easy visual novel engine and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opennovella
.RI [ command ] " " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenNovella creates and plays visual novels with branching paths, characters,
backgrounds, music, transitions and animations. Run without arguments to open
the visual editor.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "edit " [PROJECT]
Open the editor, optionally with a project.
.TP
.BI "play " PROJECT
Play a story. Options:
.B \-\-scene
.I NAME
starts at a scene,
.B \-\-fullscreen
starts in fullscreen.
.TP
.BI "new " FOLDER
Create a new project. Options:
.BI \-\-title " TITLE" ,
.BI \-\-author " NAME" ,
.BR \-\-empty .
.TP
.BI "check " PROJECT
List problems in a story. Exits with status 1 if there are errors.
.TP
.BI "export " "PROJECT OUTPUT"
Create a shareable game folder.
.TP
.BI "bugreport " [PROJECT]
Print system information for a bug report.
.PP
.I PROJECT
is a project folder or the path to its story.json.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.opennovella/editor.json
Editor settings and recent projects.
.TP
.I PROJECT/saves/
Save games, player settings and crash logs.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/opennovella/examples/demo
The demo story "The Lantern Festival".
.SH SEE ALSO
/usr/share/doc/opennovella/README.md
.SH AUTHORS
OpenNovella was created by Shawn Rapaz and Claude Code.
